  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Ok so basically i have been having this bug for about a year in VRC and its been slowly driving me absolutely mad. basically, VRC offsets my VR view to the right of the camera and this is super confusing and awful. Most of the time it is unnoticable, however when i put my hands at my sides or look down and compare my trackers and body IRL to my leg positions in game, its like everything has been shifted to the left and the movement doesnt quite match up. \nEven when I open steamvr my trackers appear to be in the correct place, unlike what VRC is telling me\nanother example is when the blue loading avatar shows up, i look straight down or straight ahead at the mirror and the blue avatar seems to be offsetted to the left as well\nthis is such a strange issue.\nits almost as if my headset is the only thing being shoved to the right of the viewpoint, and only the cameras for it, as the viewpoint itself seems to be centered.\n\nHere are examples of me putting my hands to my sides, and looking straight down. This occurs on both legacy and new FBT calibration. First image is from the mirror",
